  <title>6.3.0: Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01612</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.3.0: Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ae250c51-90ab-44a4-ab1d-dee2da9cdd86</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you will review exponent properties when dividing by monomials. You will also learn multiple methods to divide a polynomial by a binomial. You will master a method to determine the remainder of a division problem involving polynomials, as well as a method to determine if a binomial is a factor of a larger polynomial. You will also gain fluency in dividing polynomials as functions.</para>
<para>Polynomials are frequently used in calculating physics problems and other real-world situations involving projectiles and the motion of objects. Mastering the polynomial operations in this unit will help you in future studies.</para>
<para>When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Divide monomials.</item>
  <item> Divide a polynomial by a monomial.</item>
  <item> Divide polynomials using long division.</item>
  <item> Divide polynomials using synthetic division.</item>
  <item> Divide polynomial functions.</item>
  <item> Use the Remainder and Factor Theorems.</item>
</list>
<para>Here are the<emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item> 6.3.1: Dividing by Monomials</item>
  <item> 6.3.2: Dividing Polynomials Using Long Division
    <list>
      <item> 6.3.2: Self Check</item>
      <item>6.3.2: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
 </item>
  <item> 6.3.3: Dividing Polynomials Using Synthetic Division
    <list>
      <item> 6.3.3: Self Check</item>
      <item>6.3.3: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
 </item>
  <item> 6.3.4: Dividing Polynomial Functions and the Remainder Theorem
    <list>
      <item> 6.3.4: Self Check</item>
      <item>6.3.4: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
 </item>
  <item> 6.3.5: Using the Factor Theorem</item>
</list>
<para>After that, you’ll<emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list>
  <item> 6.3.6: Practice</item>
  <item> 6.3.7: Lesson Summary</item>
</list></section>
